Maintainer: Martin Jung <martinjung@zoho.com>
Description: Model the distribution of species and ecosystems in a suitability
  framing using the integrated species distribution modelling (iSDM) workflow
  described in Jung (2023) <doi:10.1016/j.ecoinf.2023.102127>. It estimates
  iSDMs from several sources of evidence, including presence-only and
  presence-absence datasets. Point-process models are used for estimating habitat
  suitability, with support for spatial latent effects and priors. The
  'ibis.iSDM' framework supports Bayesian and non-parametric machine learning
  engines, and spatial-temporal projections of habitat suitability into the
  future.
